{"title":"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(really_fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (really fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_11-20)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/380264eeecdaa2e001ecc6a81415cefc2aff6a31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> are assigned to the six faces of a cube, one number to each face. For each of the eight vertices of the cube, a product of three numbers is computed, where the three numbers are the numbers assigned to the three faces that include that vertex. What is the greatest possible value of the sum of these eight products?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/e/56e0b40f41a69edf0717127cf181c173cd4d27d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 312 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 343 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 625 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 729 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 1680$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"448\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First assign each face the letters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67f089fdbe6e5066ae93dfdec4438bc1bba0ff82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d,e,f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />. The sum of the product of the faces is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f0964c8657b987e4f96a87dc1916a7edb0a3bbf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc+acd+ade+aeb+fbc+fcd+fde+feb$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"372\" height=\"16\" />. We can factor this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cd21bd2d3785ff802bd2889ad7d11fc359e651a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+f)(b+d)(c+e)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" /> which is the product of the sum of each pair of opposite faces. In order to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adcd1ac78aad6ccfc44d8780eebd7a08efc2a448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+f)(b+c)(d+e)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" /> we use the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/9/0e9cebab460c6172b885f7cfdab87218b37337bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7+2)(6+3)(5+4) = 9^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"21\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/cedece32bb60cb67e63e24c637b5221a124745a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 729 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We'll proceed from the factoring process above.\nBy the AM-GM inequality,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa67eef8049086302c27d7648d8e0d17e704e7dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1+a_2+a_3}{3}\\geq\\sqrt[3]{a_1a_2a_3}\\]\" width=\"189\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Cubing both sides,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/233c106eb78fd6060382033db69c868915a0e2ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{a_1+a_2+a_3}{3}\\right)^3\\geq{a_1a_2a_3}\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8ff7ae5b392c1403f2bd600bb711810adbb8802.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=(a+f)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927fdd8169cdfc9fff64bf0147a3dfacc9088502.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=(b+c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93eabba6a5324e9f04a5809ad1a44684ec3816f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=(d+e)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />. Let's substitute in these values.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06d6e468f555fb1ee6e69b3607de98a90f68cee5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{a+b+c+d+e+f}{3}\\right)^3\\geq{(a+f)(b+c)(d+e)}\\]\" width=\"385\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feba0c1185391cc2b2dd3198865794e4f3c764ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d+e+f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"165\" height=\"16\" /> is fixed at 27.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42e6a5120a4a3947aa06a9123846cb6a117c1564.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{27}{3}\\right)^3\\geq{(a+f)(b+c)(d+e)}\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283da114e616eca58fa458e4073c4b6772997789.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 729 }\\geq{(a+f)(b+c)(d+e)}\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28really_fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(really_fast)\">Solution 3 (really fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (really fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we see that we want to try and maximize each vertex. Since the multiplication of each vertex is the product of three values, we want to maximize those three values. Doing so, we see that we want them to be as close as possible, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c49a5f46c513fac13dd271a7c14790547992572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.5^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> (the average of all the values). This gives us the maximum for each vertex, multiplied by the 8 vertices, yields our answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/cedece32bb60cb67e63e24c637b5221a124745a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 729 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" /> Also note that if you cannot evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c49a5f46c513fac13dd271a7c14790547992572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.5^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> quickly, a rough approximation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/047ab1a3193bc17c396ca17fc78a4b85cf709329.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5*4.5*4*8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" /> will yield 720, very close to our answer. -rayprati\n</p><p><br />\nNote about note above: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17e419a76bf7ae7e1037fa82a0fb3edf2cb00a8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.5=\\frac{9}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" /> So, we want to evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c8041867f201f9e6e65a4902b96a7777bab9b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{9}{2})^3 \\cdot 8 = \\frac{729}{8} \\cdot 8 = 729.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"189\" height=\"37\" /> So, it’s quite easy to evaluate ~solasky\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is obvious to put <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the faces that share the same vertex. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the next biggest number, the face with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has to be next to the faces with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the next biggest number, the face with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has to be next to the faces with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. making the face with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> next to the faces with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c320d4d541ddcdd74963d232e83260b50b9278b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 6 + 7 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 6 + 7 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5 + 7 \\cdot  3 \\cdot 4 + 2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 6 + 2 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 6 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5 + 2 \\cdot  3 \\cdot 4 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 729 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"683\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>Note: 1680 is impossible to achieve as it requires <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75df6ed5589ecc42533006f88abe421cf438e77f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210 = 7 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" /> for each vertex. \n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_.28Problem_11-20.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_11-20)\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fast Forward to 17:19 for problem 15\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4osvFatUv1o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4osvFatUv1o</a>\n</p><p>~THEMATHCANADIAN\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B\">2016 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017141721\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 301/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7425/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.089      1 -total\n 60.82%    7.960      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.51%    4.909      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14817:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017141721 and revision id 232963. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}